# Performance Review

## Checklist

- No expensive work (sort, filter, crypto, serialization) in hot paths or tight loops.
- No unnecessary re-computation — memoize or cache where applicable.
- No blocking I/O on responsive threads/queues.
- No large in-memory collections that could be streamed or paginated.
- Android: no unstable Compose state causing excess recompositions, Bitmap lifecycle correct.
- iOS: no main-thread work during scroll, no large images held unreduced.
- Web: no render-blocking scripts, no layout thrashing, stable list keys.
- No N+1 queries, queries use indexed columns, no unbounded SELECT.
- No chatty API patterns — batch where possible.
- Web: no whole-library imports, code splitting applied.

## Output Format

```markdown
## Performance Findings

**[P1]** `path/file.ext:line` - Title
Impact and fix direction.

## Summary
```
